Big O notation is a mathematical notation that describe the limiting
behavior of a function when the argument tends towards a particular value or infinity!

it wants to describe how a algorithm work on large data set,
we want to find out the algorithm is SCALABLE ?
an "Array" is good on finding element, bad on resizing
a  "link-list" is good on resizing, bad on finding element!
we need a concept to compare these difference.

O(1)
it means the algorithm has "CONSTANT" time
(it could be large time and different on separate machines)
but th time will not change based on size of data.

public void log (int[] numbers){
    System.out.println(numbers[0])      // the runtime complexity of this method is O(1)
}

Note: if we print more elements,
      the runtime will increase, but it remain constant         //System.out.println(numbers[0])
      so it will remain O(1)                                    //System.out.println(numbers[1])